# Cline Commit Message Rules

All commits must follow the Conventional Commits specification.

## Format

```
type(scope): subject

body

footer
```

## Allowed Types

- feat: A new feature
- fix: A bug fix
- docs: Documentation only changes
- style: Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code (white-space, formatting, missing semi-colons, etc)
- refactor: A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
- perf: A code change that improves performance
- test: Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
- chore: Changes to the build process or auxiliary tools and libraries such as documentation generation
- ci: Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
- build: Changes that affect the build system or external dependencies
- revert: Reverts a previous commit

## Required Scopes

The following scopes are required for changes in these areas:

- agents: Changes to agent-related code
- core: Changes to core system code
- config: Changes to configuration files

Other valid scopes may be used as appropriate, but agents, core, and config are mandatory for their respective domains.

## Character Limits

- Subject line: Maximum 50 characters
- Body lines: Maximum 72 characters per line
- Footer lines: Maximum 72 characters per line

## Mandatory Footer for AI-Generated Commits

All commits generated by AI must include a footer referencing the issue or task that prompted the change.

Footer format:
```
Closes #<issue-number>
```
or
```
Fixes #<issue-number>
```
or
```
Refs #<issue-number>
```

If no issue number is available, reference the task or conversation ID:
```
Refs: <task-or-conversation-id>
```

## Examples

Valid commit message:

```
feat(agents): add task planning capability

Implement hierarchical task decomposition for agents to break down complex goals into manageable subtasks.

Closes #142
```

Valid commit message:

```
fix(core): resolve race condition in event loop

Add proper locking around shared state to prevent concurrent modification exceptions.

Fixes #203
```

Valid commit message:

```
docs(config): update environment variable documentation

Closes #187
```

Invalid commit message (missing scope):

```
feat: add new feature
```

Invalid commit message (subject too long):

```
feat(agents): this subject line is way too long and exceeds the fifty character limit for commit subjects
```

Invalid commit message (missing footer for AI-generated commit):

```
fix(core): resolve null pointer exception

Add null check before accessing user profile.
```